{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 12B Problems\">2018 AMC 12B #10</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">2018 AMC 10B #14</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Statistics)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Statistics)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A list of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a46b5b3929665fcb2500f3583ab77297a85afd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> positive integers has a unique mode, which occurs exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times. What is the least number of distinct values that can occur in the list?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59da437eeeb2beed1850b5ea0dda4421dafd799f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 202\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 223\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 224\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 225\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 234$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"440\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Statistics.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Statistics)\">Solution 1 (Statistics)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Statistics)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize the number of distinct values, we want to maximize the number of times a number appears. So, we could have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> numbers appear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> number appear once, and the mode appear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, giving us a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2270f544ca1fb7d920874e37d26be08c656a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223 + 1 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 225}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"195\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Algebra)\">Solution 2 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, we want to maximize the number of time each number appears to do so. We can set up an equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/100c35be3dc28206d0bd70b998584fd8ed41c94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 9( x - 1 )\\geq2018,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of values. Notice how we can then rearrange the equation into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae095e85297a74abbbad09bb5de4705f6f891e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 ( 1 )+9 ( x - 1 )\\geq2018,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" /> which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf0cc138c0c9d4ca840673f36b9870841aa7eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 x\\geq2017,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19d73bc02f21c18a8f365d500e186b93948cb2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq224\\frac19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> We cannot have a fraction of a value so we must round up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8efdf979f6ec9795e0dbd88e400fa307582add.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 225}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Username_taken12\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a unique number \\( n \\) with a mode of 10. This means we have 2008 terms left. We see that \\( \\lfloor 2008/9 \\rfloor = 223 \\), with remainder 1. Our answer is simply \\( 223 + 1 + 1 =\\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8efdf979f6ec9795e0dbd88e400fa307582add.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 225}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/M-z7SJwlsLY\">https://youtu.be/M-z7SJwlsLY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B\">2018 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Probl